%S A401174 2,4,6,8,0,2,8,24,64,30,104,8,18,10,48,256,940,2336,6464,10616,18984,
%T A401174 17680,7882,320,12,80,640,4420,25744,141680,662820,3071048,12216080
%N A401174 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of Boolean functions of n variables whose minimum AND-inverter graph size is k, for 0 <= k <= A057241(n).
%C A401174 The cost metric is that of A057241 (R. C. Schroeppel): 2-input AND gates cost 1, NOT is free, fanout is free, inputs and the constants 0 and 1 are free, no feedback is allowed. Such circuits are known as AND-inverter graphs (AIGs).
%C A401174 Functions are counted as truth tables, all 2^(2^n) of them, including those that do not depend on all n variables; nothing is identified under symmetry. T(n,0) = 2*n + 2 counts the 2 constants and the 2*n literals. Complementing the output is free, so every term is even.
%C A401174 Row sums are 2^(2^n) = A001146(n), and row n has A057241(n)+1 terms. Rows 0..4 are complete; of row 5 only T(5,k) for k <= 8 is known, and A057241(5) is not known either, so the length of row 5 is open: the table of a(5,c) by David Ian Stevenson in A057241, the number of NPN classes of 5-variable functions of cost c, puts A057241(5) at 16 or 17.
%C A401174 T(2,2) = 0: no function of 2 variables needs exactly 2 AND gates; XOR and XNOR need 3.
%C A401174 Rows 0..4 come from the minimum AIG sizes of the 222 NPN classes of 4-variable functions (equivalence under permuting the inputs, complementing the inputs and complementing the output; A000370(4) = 222) and their orbit sizes. The class values are those of the catalog in the repository krinkin/bounds, independently recomputed here with a SAT encoder, which agrees on all 222; the two entries that the catalog gave only as upper bounds, 0x1669 and 0x166b, were certified exact here by the matching lower bound, a DRAT-checked UNSAT proof that 9 gates do not suffice, and the catalog was updated accordingly. The numbers of NPN classes of cost k for n = 4 are 2, 1, 2, 7, 9, 24, 30, 61, 45, 37, 4; the 4 classes of cost 10 are those found by R. C. Schroeppel (see A057241).
%C A401174 The terms T(5,0) through T(5,8) were computed by two programs that share no code. The first enumerates sequences of gates, either all of them (k <= 6) or with the first gate fixed to x0 AND x1 and the result closed under the 3840 permutations and negations of the inputs (k <= 8); for k = 8 a second choice of first gate, ~x3 AND ~x4, gives the same set. The second enumerates unordered sets of gate functions, reduced under the same group at every depth, and completes the last three gates exhaustively. The two programs give the same sets of functions for k = 6, 7, 8, bit for bit, and the same counts for k <= 5.
%C A401174 The numbers of NPN classes of cost k for n = 5 are 2, 1, 2, 7, 21, 55, 198, 667, 2311 for k = 0..8. They agree with Stevenson's table of a(5,c) in A057241, read with constants of cost 0 (the convention the table attributes to Knuth).
%C A401174 Partial sums of row 5 (functions of 5 variables computable with at most k AND gates): 12, 92, 732, 5152, 30896, 172576, 835396, 3906444, 16122524; the last is about 0.375% of 2^32.
%H A401174 Luiz Antonio Busnello, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23406952">Boolean functions of five variables by minimum AND-inverter graph size, sizes 0 to 8: two enumeration programs, counts and run records</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401174 Kirill Krinkin, <a href="https://github.com/krinkin/bounds">Minimum AIG sizes of the 222 NPN classes of 4-variable Boolean functions</a>, GitHub repository.
%H A401174 <a href="/index/Bo#Boolean">Index entries for sequences related to Boolean functions</a>
%F A401174 Row n sums to 2^(2^n) = A001146(n).
%e A401174 Triangle begins:
%e A401174   n=0: 2;
%e A401174   n=1: 4;
%e A401174   n=2: 6, 8, 0, 2;
%e A401174   n=3: 8, 24, 64, 30, 104, 8, 18;
%e A401174   n=4: 10, 48, 256, 940, 2336, 6464, 10616, 18984, 17680, 7882, 320;
%e A401174   n=5: 12, 80, 640, 4420, 25744, 141680, 662820, 3071048, 12216080, ...
%e A401174 T(1,0) = 4: the 2 constants and the 2 literals x, ~x, none of which needs a gate.
%e A401174 T(5,1) = 80: the functions l_i AND l_j, for literals l_i, l_j of two distinct variables, number binomial(5,2)*4 = 40, and their complements (ORs of two literals) are another 40.
%Y A401174 Cf. A000370, A001146, A056287, A057241, A058759.
